1021066,ca.proc.d.1934-03-14.2.10.76,1934-03-14,b11f5b30-7d32-44e6-b23c-a24561c1eaf5,ca.m.7719,Mr. MACKENZIE KING:,Leader of the Official Opposition,QUESTIONS,"TITLES, HONOURS AND AWARDS PROPOSAL THAT PRIME MINISTER REFRAIN FROM RECOMMENDING TITLES FOR CANADIANS",,"May I ask the Prime Minister a question before we leave this matter? According to his interpretation of a private member's resolution the resolution applies only for the one parliament; it would not have been effective beyond the present parliament had it carried?

